        "heading": "3. \"For men there is a share of...",
        "text": "\"For men there is a share of what they earned, and for women, there is a share of what they earned...\" (Al-Nisa: 32)\n\nSimilarly, in his farewell sermon, The Rasool of mercy () clearly emphasized upon the equality of men and women,saying, \"Indeed you have rights over your wives and your wives have rights over you\" (Sunan al-Tirmidhi Vol. 1, Book 7, Hadith 1163) As clear as day is the fact that with the exclusion of the half of its population, Pakistan cannot reach the pinnacle of progress, peace and stability. In the words of Quaide Azam Muhammad Ali Jinnah,\" No Nation can rise to the heights of glory unless her women stand side by side with men.\"\n\n\"Thus, in order to keep the wheel of progress and development rolling on, the latent potentialities of women need to be utilised by ensuring gender parity in all walks of life.\n\n1- Journal of prevention and intervention in the community< vol;48,2020-issue 4: Gender inequalities: implications and resistance.",
